          deckDescription: 'A standard 52-card French deck with no jokers. The full pack is used for Hockey: each of three periods uses the entire deck, dealt in batches of five cards per player per deal, with a final deal of six cards each so that all cards are used.',
          suitDescription: 'The four French suits (hearts, diamonds, clubs, spades) are used; each suit has thirteen cards. In Hockey, capture is by matching the rank of the face-up card on the table, and the thematic terminology (breakaways, saves, goals) is applied to these captures.',
          rankDescription: "Standard ranks from Ace through King in each suit; numeric cards 2 through 10 plus Jack, Queen, and Ace. In Hockey, when a player plays a card that matches the rank of the card on the table, they capture it (a 'goal'); otherwise the card is saved and remains on the table.",
